WEBVTT

NOTE
Disc 1, Scene 29h: Lunar Gate launch sequence
Duration: ~46 seconds
Source: FF8 Gameplay/Cutscene
Describes the climactic launch of the pod carrying Squall and the comatose Rinoa toward the Lunar Base orbiting the moon

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
A massive underground facility comes into view. The Lunar Gate is revealed — a facility of immense scale built into the earth. Enormous electromagnetic launch rails extend horizontally into the distance, creating a tunnel of metal and technology. The rails gleam beneath floodlights.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
A sleek, white launch pod is being carefully loaded onto the rail system. Squall stands inside or near the pod, his expression grim and determined. Rinoa lies comatose within the pod, protected and secured for the journey. Esthar personnel in futuristic clothing work around the pod with precision.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The pod is fully positioned on the electromagnetic rail. The launch mechanism is engaged. A low hum begins — power building in the system. The air itself seems to vibrate. Lights along the rail begin to glow, building in intensity.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The electromagnetic charge reaches critical levels. The rails begin to glow with blue and white energy. The hum becomes a roar. Squall grips the interior of the pod, preparing for launch. The pressure builds to an almost unbearable intensity.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
The launch sequence activates. The pod accelerates along the rail with incredible force. The acceleration is instantaneous and violent — the pod becomes a blur of motion. The rails beneath blur. The tunnel streaks past at unimaginable speed.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The pod exits the underground facility. The camera follows as the pod shoots upward at a steep angle, still accelerating. The Esthar facility drops away below. The landscape of the planet recedes rapidly as the pod climbs.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The blue sky of the planet is visible around the ascending pod. The atmosphere is thick and visible. The pod continues to climb, leaving the habitable world behind. The curvature of the planet begins to become visible at the pod's trajectory.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The sky darkens from blue to deep purple to black. Stars begin to appear — thousands of points of light scattered across the void. The pod enters the vacuum of space, moving with unstoppable momentum. The atmosphere below now forms a thin blue line — the boundary between the living world and the void.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The planet is now visible in its entirety below the pod's trajectory. A vast, beautiful sphere of blue, white, and brown. Clouds swirl across the surface. Continents and oceans are visible from this perspective. The planet shrinks as the pod hurtles away.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The stars fill the view now. The pod streaks through space — a tiny human artifact hurtling through the cosmic void toward its destination. The silence of space is broken only by the pod's engines. The moon looms ahead, growing larger.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
The final moments of the launch sequence. The pod approaches the moon. The lunar surface fills the view — a gray, cratered landscape, lifeless and alien. The Lunar Base becomes visible — a space station in orbit, its modular structure silhouetted against the moon and stars.
